From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_RESERVE_TABLES=1|<slots>: the texture and buffer caches' slot tables at full size at boot; EDEN_UP_RESERVE_SCRATCH_MIB=<n>: the upload scratch too; off by default (KEEPS THE STORE)

Store: KEEPS THE STORE. texture_cache.h, texture_cache_base.h and buffer_cache.h change; none is among
the translation id's 418 inputs (the 292 core-source inputs compared byte for byte, T172 core against
this one, in the VM: 0 differ; the rewritten vk_pipeline_cache_cost.cpp is byte for byte T172's), and
the two switch names are new, not in TranslationSwitches.

Switches: EDEN_UP_RESERVE_TABLES=1 (4096 slots) or =<slots> (1024 to 65536; unset, 0 or anything
else: off). EDEN_UP_RESERVE_SCRATCH_MIB=<n> (9 to 64; unset or anything else: off, 8 MiB as before).
Lines (stderr, once at boot): "EDEN_UP_RESERVE_TABLES texture cache: ..." and "... buffer cache: ...".

Why: every slot table doubles in one allocation of the whole new table, inside the frame that wants
the slot. run1395 died on the image table's 2048 -> 4096 doubling at the load into the area past the
field (one 10,354,696 byte request, the pool at 1-2 MiB in one piece). run1397 (the survivor) passed
2048 images in the same window (1606 at census t 170.3, 2143 at 173.4) and found the room. Most
images the censuses of 13 Nov counted: 2302 (run1397), 2071-2162 in run1395/1398/1399/1400. Most
buffers counted alive: 931 (EDEN_REFUSED_BUFFERS, run1395). The heap site tables show the image
table's block (9 MiB, Reserve at 0x174ff1c) in run1399; no other table is large enough to be listed
(the list starts at 8 MiB).

What (at boot, TextureCache and BufferCache constructors, right after the null entries):
- images, views, allocations, map views: <slots>; samplers, framebuffers: <slots>/4; buffers <slots>/2.
- At 4096, with T166's slot sizes (disassembly of each Reserve): images 4096 x 2528 B = 9.9 MiB,
  views 4096 x 936 B = 3.7 MiB, framebuffers 1024 x 656 B = 0.64 MiB, samplers 1024 x 176 B = 0.17
  MiB, allocations 4096 x 24 B = 0.09 MiB, map views 4096 x 32 B = 0.13 MiB, buffers 2048 x 320 B =
  0.63 MiB: about 15.3 MiB of heap at boot, plus 4 bytes a slot of free list. Without the switch the
  image table alone reaches 4096 slots (9.9 MiB) at this load anyway, and 2048 (4.9 MiB) in the
  field; the line gives the sizes of this build.
- A table that fills up still doubles as before (0892 then makes the image and buffer cases a
  refusal instead of the end).
- The upload scratch (swizzle_data_buffer: UploadImageContents reads guest memory into it) starts at
  EDEN_UP_RESERVE_SCRATCH_MIB. It grows to the largest image uploaded, releasing first with
  EDEN_AREA_CHANGE_SCRATCH_RELEASE=1 (on in our settings): one heap request of that size when
  a large image comes. Seen: 15-16 MiB in run1395's site table before the load (stderr 572), a 32
  MiB block at the load in run1399 (its crash log 1060). TickFrame's trims are
  unchanged below the reserve; the scratch keeps its reserved size through them (with our
  EDEN_TC_SCRATCH_KEEP_MIB=16 a 32 MiB scratch was freed at the first frame; that name is in
  TranslationSwitches, so raising it instead would RESET THE STORE).

Review fix (13 Nov, reviewer): the first version reserved before the null entries. A table reserved
while empty hands out its last slot first (the free list pops from the back), so the null image,
view, sampler and buffer went to slot 4095/1023/2047 while NULL_IMAGE_ID, NULL_IMAGE_VIEW_ID,
NULL_SAMPLER_ID and NULL_BUFFER_ID (types.h line 28-32, buffer_cache_base.h line 108) name slot 0:
an empty slot. Native test of the console's slot_vector.h: reserve first, null at 4095; null first,
null at 0. Now the tables are reserved after the null entries.

Not checked: the view, sampler and framebuffer counts (not in any log); a build; the console.
T173 note: 0885 also changes texture_cache.h and texture_cache_base.h; this patch's hunks are the
constructor (and two functions before it) and a declaration after ApplyThresholdOverrides, away from
0885's (ShortPoolCollect, AreaEvict's end, TickFrame, UnmapMemory, JoinImages, the members).
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
index cf7092a3e2..c543d5fde0 100644
--- a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
@@ -59,6 +59,22 @@ BufferCache<P>::BufferCache(Tegra::MaxwellDeviceMemoryManager& device_memory_, R
     }
     // Ensure the first slot is used for the null buffer
     void(slot_buffers.insert(runtime, NullBufferParams{}));
+    // EDEN_UP_RESERVE_TABLES (0891, texture_cache.h ReserveTableSlots): the buffer table at half
+    // the texture cache's size (the most buffers counted alive in the 13 Nov loads: 931,
+    // EDEN_REFUSED_BUFFERS in run1395), so it does not double during an area load. After the null
+    // buffer: a table reserved while empty hands out its last slot first; NULL_BUFFER_ID is slot 0.
+    if (const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_UP_RESERVE_TABLES");
+        value != nullptr && value[0] >= '1' && value[0] <= '9') {
+        char* end = nullptr;
+        const unsigned long long asked = std::strtoull(value, &end, 10);
+        const unsigned long long slots = asked == 1 ? 4096 : asked;
+        if (end != value && *end == '\0' && slots >= 1024 && slots <= 65536) {
+            slot_buffers.reserve(static_cast<size_t>(slots / 2));
+            std::fprintf(stderr, "EDEN_UP_RESERVE_TABLES buffer cache: buffers %zu x %zu B: %zu KiB\n",
+                         slot_buffers.capacity(), sizeof(Buffer),
+                         (slot_buffers.capacity() * sizeof(Buffer)) >> 10);
+        }
+    }
     gpu_modified_ranges.Clear();
     inline_buffer_id = NULL_BUFFER_ID;
 #ifdef YUZU_LEGACY
diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
index dc0c9b0a39..770a7dd3c1 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
@@ -437,6 +437,95 @@ template <typename Runtime>
     return std::optional{runtime.UploadStagingBuffer(size)};
 }
 
+// EDEN_UP_RESERVE_TABLES=1 or =<slots> (0891; 1024 to 65536, digits only; 1 means 4096; unset, 0
+// or anything else: off, the tables grow by doubling as before). The texture cache's slot tables
+// start at that size instead of growing 1, 2, 4, ... slots: each doubling is one allocation of the
+// whole new table, inside the frame that needed the slot. run1395 (13 Nov, T166, the load into the
+// area past the field) ended there: the image table went from 2048 to 4096 slots, one 10,354,696
+// byte request (2528 bytes a slot), with the pool's largest free piece at 1-2 MiB; EDEN_NEW_WAIT gave
+// up after 2000 ms and the program ended (SlotVector::Reserve is noexcept upstream). The censuses of
+// the six starts of that batch and the next counted at most 2302 images (run1397, t 177.6), 2071-2162
+// in the others. Images, views, allocations and map views get <slots>, samplers and framebuffers a
+// quarter (their counts are not in the logs; not checked). The buffer cache reads the same switch
+// (buffer_cache.h). Slot sizes in T166's build: image 2528, view 936, framebuffer 656, sampler 176,
+// allocation 24, map view 32 bytes: about 14.6 MiB at 4096 (images 9.9, views 3.7), taken once at
+// boot. A table that fills up still doubles as before. One line at boot.
+inline u32 ReserveTableSlots() {
+    static const u32 slots = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_UP_RESERVE_TABLES");
+        if (value == nullptr || value[0] < '0' || value[0] > '9') {
+            return u32{0};
+        }
+        char* end = nullptr;
+        const unsigned long long asked = std::strtoull(value, &end, 10);
+        if (end == value || *end != '\0' || asked == 0) {
+            return u32{0};
+        }
+        if (asked == 1) {
+            return u32{4096};
+        }
+        if (asked < 1024 || asked > 65536) {
+            std::fprintf(stderr, "EDEN_UP_RESERVE_TABLES=%s is not 1 or 1024 to 65536: off\n", value);
+            return u32{0};
+        }
+        return static_cast<u32>(asked);
+    }();
+    return slots;
+}
+
+// EDEN_UP_RESERVE_SCRATCH_MIB=<n> (0891; 9 to 64, digits only; unset or anything else: off, 8 MiB as
+// before): the upload scratch (swizzle_data_buffer, which UploadImageContents reads guest memory
+// into) starts at n MiB. It grows to the largest image the game uploads, releasing first with
+// EDEN_AREA_CHANGE_SCRATCH_RELEASE=1: a heap request of that size at the moment a large image comes,
+// often an area load. Seen in the heap's site table: 15-16 MiB (run1395, before the load) and one
+// 32 MiB block at the load (run1399, its crash log line 1060). The trims in
+// TickFrame are unchanged (EDEN_TC_SCRATCH_KEEP_MIB, EDEN_UP_HEAP_HOLDERS may free it again).
+inline size_t ReserveScratchBytes() {
+    static const size_t bytes = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_UP_RESERVE_SCRATCH_MIB");
+        if (value == nullptr || value[0] < '0' || value[0] > '9') {
+            return size_t{0};
+        }
+        char* end = nullptr;
+        const unsigned long long mib = std::strtoull(value, &end, 10);
+        if (end == value || *end != '\0' || mib < 9 || mib > 64) {
+            return size_t{0};
+        }
+        return static_cast<size_t>(mib) << 20;
+    }();
+    return bytes;
+}
+
+template <class P>
+void TextureCache<P>::ReserveTables() {
+    const u32 slots = ReserveTableSlots();
+    if (slots == 0) {
+        return;
+    }
+    const u32 quarter = slots / 4;
+    slot_images.reserve(slots);
+    slot_image_views.reserve(slots);
+    slot_image_allocs.reserve(slots);
+    slot_map_views.reserve(slots);
+    slot_samplers.reserve(quarter);
+    slot_framebuffers.reserve(quarter);
+    const size_t bytes = slot_images.capacity() * sizeof(Image) +
+                         slot_image_views.capacity() * sizeof(ImageView) +
+                         slot_image_allocs.capacity() * sizeof(ImageAlloc) +
+                         slot_map_views.capacity() * sizeof(ImageMapView) +
+                         slot_samplers.capacity() * sizeof(Sampler) +
+                         slot_framebuffers.capacity() * sizeof(Framebuffer);
+    std::fprintf(stderr,
+                 "EDEN_UP_RESERVE_TABLES texture cache: images %zu x %zu B, views %zu x %zu B, "
+                 "allocations %zu, map views %zu, samplers %zu x %zu B, framebuffers %zu x %zu B: "
+                 "%zu KiB; upload scratch %zu KiB\n",
+                 slot_images.capacity(), sizeof(Image), slot_image_views.capacity(),
+                 sizeof(ImageView), slot_image_allocs.capacity(), slot_map_views.capacity(),
+                 slot_samplers.capacity(), sizeof(Sampler), slot_framebuffers.capacity(),
+                 sizeof(Framebuffer), bytes >> 10,
+                 (std::max)(size_t{8} << 20, ReserveScratchBytes()) >> 10);
+}
+
 template <class P>
 TextureCache<P>::TextureCache(Runtime& runtime_, Tegra::MaxwellDeviceMemoryManager& device_memory_)
     : runtime{runtime_}, device_memory{device_memory_} {
@@ -468,7 +557,8 @@ TextureCache<P>::TextureCache(Runtime& runtime_, Tegra::MaxwellDeviceMemoryManag
     // These values were chosen based on typical peak swizzle data sizes seen in some titles
     constexpr size_t SWIZZLE_DATA_BUFFER_INITIAL_CAPACITY = 8_MiB;
     constexpr size_t UNSWIZZLE_DATA_BUFFER_INITIAL_CAPACITY = 1_MiB;
-    swizzle_data_buffer.resize_destructive(SWIZZLE_DATA_BUFFER_INITIAL_CAPACITY);
+    swizzle_data_buffer.resize_destructive(
+        (std::max)(SWIZZLE_DATA_BUFFER_INITIAL_CAPACITY, ReserveScratchBytes()));
     unswizzle_data_buffer.resize_destructive(UNSWIZZLE_DATA_BUFFER_INITIAL_CAPACITY);
     // EDEN_UP_WRITEBACK_BANDS (util.cpp): its kept write-back buffer, made once here when the
     // switch is on at boot. It is not a ScratchBuffer, so the trims in TickFrame never free it.
@@ -480,6 +570,12 @@ TextureCache<P>::TextureCache(Runtime& runtime_, Tegra::MaxwellDeviceMemoryManag
     void(slot_image_views.insert(runtime, NullImageViewParams{}));
     void(slot_samplers.insert(runtime, sampler_descriptor));
 
+    // EDEN_UP_RESERVE_TABLES (0891): the slot tables at their full size now, while the pool has
+    // room, so none of them doubles in one large allocation during an area load. After the null
+    // resources: a table reserved while empty hands out its last slot first, and NULL_IMAGE_ID,
+    // NULL_IMAGE_VIEW_ID and NULL_SAMPLER_ID are slot 0.
+    ReserveTables();
+
     // EDEN_UP_AREA_BUDGET: its first use, so AreaEvict and JoinImages can Peek it.
     static_cast<void>(Common::LiveSwitch::Value<Common::LiveSwitch::Id::AreaBudget>());
 
@@ -2018,8 +2114,12 @@ void TextureCache<P>::TickFrame() {
     }();
     for (auto* const scratch : {&swizzle_data_buffer, &unswizzle_data_buffer}) {
         static const bool trim = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_HEAP_HOLDERS");
-        if (scratch->capacity() > scratch_keep ||
-            (trim && (frame_tick & 255) == 0 && scratch->capacity() > (size_t{8} << 20))) {
+        // EDEN_UP_RESERVE_SCRATCH_MIB (0891): the upload scratch keeps its boot size between
+        // frames; else EDEN_TC_SCRATCH_KEEP_MIB=16 (ours) frees a 32 MiB one at once.
+        const size_t reserved = scratch == &swizzle_data_buffer ? ReserveScratchBytes() : 0;
+        if (scratch->capacity() > (std::max)(scratch_keep, reserved) ||
+            (trim && (frame_tick & 255) == 0 &&
+             scratch->capacity() > (std::max)(size_t{8} << 20, reserved))) {
             scratch->release();
         }
     }
